what's up squidows and welcome back to  the fifth lesson  of economics my name is joey and today  we're going to be talking about the  newest weapon  in splatoon 2 the splat brella now we've  all had the chance to play around with  it for the last two weeks or so  and it's an interesting weapon for a  variety of different reasons  the most obvious one being its unique  secondary fire we'll get to those  specifics a little bit later in the  video  but for now if you're still not sure  which weapon to really use  you can check out the other economics  videos in which i talk about salmon run  other weapons to use you know a  breakdown of which one is  best for you uh even gear if you'd like  so far all the economics lessons have  been about an  all-encompassing aspect of the game but  this lesson will be  all about the splat brella because i  feel it introduces enough new abilities  and  techniques to kind of warn its own video  but anyway let's talk about how it feels  to use  [Music]  now umbrellas are the first brand new  weapon type  in splatoon 2 which means they have  their own victory pose they  are completely different from all the  other weapons in the game but that  doesn't mean they  don't share some similar qualities with  other weapons  for example the gun itself fires a short  to mid-range shotgun blast  and it's not a rapid-fire weapon meaning  that it's kind of similar to a slosher  in that you'll need to pull the trigger  for every single shot  also similar to a slosher is that it  kills in two direct hits  so if you're at point blank range two  trigger pulls  they'll be splatted and also also  similar to a slosher is the brella's ink  spread  now it'll lay down a patch of ink with a  good size radius and  along with it a wide trail behind it now  this makes  umbrellas really good for inking you can  cover some ground really quickly  and for comparison this is what the ink  spread looks like  compared with the standard blaster on  the left and the standard slosher  on the right so you can kind of see it's  it's very similar and very good for  inking  but let's get into the real reason  behind using the brella which is the  shield here  pressing and holding the trigger will  open up the umbrella and  that shield that opens up will guard you  from incoming ink  now this is a good way to protect  against head-on attackers  it can block a majority of special  attacks and most weapons  it doesn't protect against everything  like if you have someone going  head-on at you unloading a bunch of ink  it will break down and they will be able  to splat you  but it can withstand quite a bit of  punishment now i'll probably have to do  a little bit more testing after this but  right now it looks like it can withstand  a lot  uh but one thing to keep in mind when  using the brella is that you walk  really slow when you open it similar to  aiming with a charger or revving up a  splatling  you won't be able to move that much but  you want to be able to  use that shield to your advantage once  an enemy inkling sees it and they know  they can't bust  through it they may try to you know swim  around you and that's when you drop the  brella  drop the shield and splat them when  they're in the ink but of course that's  not all that the brellas can do if you  continue holding the trigger eventually  you'll launch the shield portion which  travels in the straight line  on the ground and it leaves behind a  trail of ink that you can safely swim  behind  now the speed is not quite as fast as  say  a curling bomb and i wouldn't say it's  the most  ideal way to travel like there is that  delay before the shield actually  launches  that kind of negates the speed increase  that you get from swimming behind it  so i wouldn't say it's the fastest way  to go but if you're traveling across  un-ink territory it's not a terrible  idea one tactic  i actually like doing is launching the  brella towards an enemy and then you  hide in the ink  and see if they attack the brella  because most of the time when you see it  coming towards you  you you assume that the the person  launching it is going to be swimming  right behind it  so they might chase after the umbrella  in which case you can pop up  splat them and then be on your merry way  and so for this last portion i kind of  want to talk about  my thoughts and kind of opinions on the  brella  and i'll be honest the first couple  games that i actually played with this i  ended up  getting zero splats it was mostly  because i was experimenting and  kind of seeing what the weapon could do  but i feel like brellas will typically  not get the most splats in the game like  i don't think that they're the most  offensive weapons and they do have a  wide spread but their fire rate is  kind of slow it's not like a tri-slosher  where you can you know get them in two  hits  right away you know if i'm chasing  someone and i don't hit them  at point-blank range it's going to take  me way more shots than just two in order  to splat them  i also don't think that they have quite  the range to compete with  you know other sloshers or even other  weapons you know like a splattershot pro  is going to outrange it  you know a blaster is probably a closer  comparison to the brella  uh with the delay in between the shots  and the emphasis on  accuracy over you know rushing someone  down  but i feel like the shield is where  you'll succeed the most  your approach is going to be very  similar to a splatling like you're going  to be  backing up the shooters in the front  people taking point  will probably rely on you to cover them  you can also like survey the landscape  and then spot a location that you want  to move to  or if you see an enemy inkling in a duel  with one of your teammates you can  launch the brella towards them  and then swim behind it and try to  surprise them there like overall if you  use a brella you'll probably be in a  more supporting role than like in the  front lines  you know it is a satisfying weapon to  get splats with but the best way to use  it i think is  probably flanking and you know coming at  people from the sides behind them  so you can get a direct hit and splat  them really easily  now as for recommendations for abilities  on your gear i will say  ink saver for sure now when just  shooting it normally  it doesn't drain too much ink but it's  when you open up the umbrella  hold it out and launch the shield that's  going to drain a third of your tank  and if you're caught trying to use the  shield without enough ink you'll end up  putting it away and being  a sitting duck for your enemies to splat  you now the standard splat brella comes  with  a sprinkler sub weapon which makes it a  good support for your team  and it has probably the most fitting  special weapon with the ink storm  there's nothing really too complex with  this loadout both of these  uh abilities are best used for  reclaiming and maintaining territory  uh you want to use ink storm usually  right away once you get it  there's no reason to hold on to the ink  storm you just want to throw it out as  soon as you get it  and as for the sprinkler just make sure  you use it generously you want to throw  it on top of  high ledges on top of walls to make sure  it rains down as much ink  as possible alright so that should cover  just about all you need to know to get  started with the umbrella uh for now at  least  people i'm sure will be coming up with  strategies as i get more familiar with  the weapon  so i hope you guys enjoyed this latest  economics lesson  uh i want to thank you guys all for the  comments questions  and discussions about the game you know  it's hard for me to know everything  and you guys have been super helpful in  the comments patching the holes in my  knowledge  now i know nintendo's about to drop a  couple of huge updates including new  stages for turf war  salmon run and the bubble blower special  and i'll be back in a couple of weeks to  talk about those  but in the meantime if you have any  suggestions for the next lesson  anything that you're dying to learn  about the game you can write in the  comments below or ask me on twitter at  uncle fuzz  so again thanks for watching and i'll  see you squids next time
 

